WIP, does not build. Apply on top of 0002, 0003 and 0004 (ib-mcs 8fb8986eb + 0004).

Goal: LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_SWAP=1. The MoE cache banks live at the top of the CUDA compute buffer, above what graphs
of up to 32 tokens use. Batches larger than 32 tokens (prefill) overwrite them, so decode gets the copy space of
prefill as extra cache. Measured potential: 35.1-35.2 tok/s decode (ub 16 + 600-850 MiB cache) while prefill
keeps ub 384 (419 tok/s), vs 32.7 for the recommended 32K line.

Done in this patch:
- ggml_gallocr_get_buffer and ggml_backend_sched_get_buffer (the single-chunk compute buffer of a backend).
- llama_moe_cache::max_batch made public, swap_enabled/swap_place/swap_phase/swap_check declared.
- llama_context::sched_reserve: with swap, reserve a 32-token graph first, record the buffer size per backend
  (lo), and call swap_place after the final pp reserve.
- process_ubatch: swap_phase(n_tokens) before the graph, swap_check after ggml_backend_sched_alloc_graph.

Still to write in llama-moe-cache.cpp:
- getenv LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_SWAP; with swap, allocate the device banks with a dummy buffer (alloc_buf with
  no_alloc = true), skip the clear.
- lru.clear_slots(): empty canon, key_of, the lists and the slot maps, n_filled = 0, keep crf/last_use/clock.
- swap_place: per device, banks at (buffer size - bank bytes) aligned down, must be >= lo + 16 MiB; set each
  bank's data, then each view's data = view_src->data + view_offs; memset the banks to 0; clear_slots.
- swap_phase: n_tokens > max_batch -> clear_slots once (dirty); first small batch after -> sched synchronize,
  memset banks to 0 (zero slots), dirty = false. The cache refills by uploads while not full.
- swap_check: if the compute buffer moved or grew, swap_place again with the stored lo.
- The three method bodies of the public class forwarding to pimpl.
Risk to check: the tensor->buffer of the banks stays the 1-byte dummy CUDA buffer (WEIGHTS usage) while data
points into the compute buffer; uploads and memsets go through tensor->data, so this should hold. Gate with KLD.

